This colossal statue of the king of Mount Olympus is quite a sight. Though many of the other non-time-traveling onlookers seem to think the chryselephantine (ivory and gold) material of the statue is a bit archaic. Of course, to you, I suppose everything around here looks archaic. Though the statue is quite grand (said to be the third largest collosal statue in its time), it is not the solution to your labyrintine adventure.